{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Linescan colour and Xray Linescan channel select}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Linescan_colour_and_Xray_Linescan_channel_selec}
\pard \fs36 Linescan colour and Xray Linescan channel select
\par \fs24 
\par When a\b  linescan profile window\plain\fs24  is on display right click to show popup menu.
\par The colour of the trace may be selected.
\par 
\par When an \b X-Ray linescan profile window\plain\fs24  is on display right click to show popup menu.
\par The colour of the trace may be selected.
\par The X-Ray Linescan channel may be selected.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Point to point reduced format}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Point_to_point_reduced_format}
\pard \fs36 Point to point reduced format
\par \fs24 For a Point to Point measurement object there are associated two results parameters, the distance and the angle.
\par These results are displayed in the results panel.
\par This may be modified as follows
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \tab Select the line between the point to point markers
\par \tab Right mouse button click to display pop up menu
\par \tab Select \b Properties\plain\fs24  - \b Results\plain\fs24 
\par 
\par \pard\tx355 Alternatively double click on the results panel.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 With the resulting dialog you may select any combination of the results parameters required.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 If no parameters are selected the Point to Point object will display in reduced format.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 i.e.\tab  No labels to identify the object.
\par \tab The\b  value only\plain\fs24  of the distance is displayed near the centre of the dotted line.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Relative Stage Movement}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} N9DA_}
\pard \fs36 Relative Stage Movement
\par \fs24 The parameters \b Stage Delta X\plain\fs24 , \b Stage Delta Y\plain\fs24 , \b Stage Delta Z\plain\fs24 , \b Stage Delta T\plain\fs24 , \b Stage Delta R\plain\fs24 , \b Stage Delta M\plain\fs24  
\par have been added. Setting any of them to a value (positive or negative) will add this delta value to the current axis position
\par and perform a \b GoTo \plain\fs24 for the axis. These parameters may be used in macros.
\par 
\par In addition on the Stage tab of the SEM Control panel are a set of \b Delta\plain\fs24  buttons which when pressed will allow entry of the above parameter values.
\par \page
