{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} V01.00 New}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} V01.00_New}
\pard \fs36 V01.00 New (since Beta3)
\par \fs24 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 1. New dialog added for Water Flow/Temperature status
\par 2. New Gun Monitor Utility (Service Use only)
\par 3. Enhancement to \uldb Image Gallery\plain\fs24 {\v Contents@gallery.hlp} to allow printing of multiple images on a page (ctrl click for multiple selection) 
\par 4. All main sections of Help included, support for F1 and shift F1 help added.
\par 5. New macro special function to save stage position in label "Current"
\par 6. New Macro special functions to switch full screen mode on/off (equivalent to Shift F3)
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 7. New Macro special function to move cursor off screen
\par 8. Macro Message instruction extended to permit Yes/No selection
\par 9. New Macro Instruction to execute a program
\par 10. \uldb Standard Conditions\plain\fs24 {\v Z1JVVC@leom.hlp} function added to Macro Engine
\par 11. Stage Co-ordinate store/recall points list data may now be viewed and edited.
\par 12. New parameters added for \ul Relative Stage Movement\plain\fs24 {\v N9DA_}
\par 13. \ul Point to point reduced format\plain\fs24 {\v Point_to_point_reduced_format}
\par 14. \ul Linescan colour and Xray Linescan channel select\plain\fs24 {\v Linescan_colour_and_Xray_Linescan_channel_selec}
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 15. Image Gallery now has a Delete file Facility.
\par 16. Trial version of Stage Registration functions included(Note a licence is required for use).
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} V01.00 Restrictions}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} V01.00_Restrictions}
\pard\tx355 \fs36 V01.00 Restrictions and known problems
\par \pard\tx355 \fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 The following restrictions/problems apply to this release:
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 1.\tab X-Ray line scanning and dotmaps are not fully tested.
\par 2.\tab Certain sections of the on-line help are not complete.
\par 3.\tab Support for the French and German language is only partially supported.
\par 4\tab On systems upgraded from Beta releases switching on User Magnification calibration without first performing a calibration results in an erroneous magnification.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} V01.00 User Actions}
