{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} V02.03 Bugs Fixed}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} V02.03_Bugs_Fixed}
\pard \fs36 V02.03 Bugs Fixed since V02.02
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \fs24 1.\fs36 \tab \fs24  LEO 1450 only. Unable to configure QBSD, SCM, TRANS detectors.
\par 2.\tab  Crash on image load. 
\par 3.\tab  Stage Control graphic - direction of rotation corrected.
\par 4.\tab  'Start' Macro failed to execute under NT
\par 5.\tab  RemCon32 failed to handle $CSOF command
\par 6.\tab  Macro editor allowed selection of some invalid state values.
\par 7.\tab  RemCon failed to save Comms settings.
\par 8.\tab If windows focus on SEM Control,Stage Control or dialogs some shortcuts were lost.
\par 9.\tab Clipboard paste failed under NT.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 10.\tab LEO 400 Series with cartesian 95 stage. Under some circumstances the joystick would only drive the stage very slowly.
\par 11.\tab LEO 1400VP Series only: Saving state altered VPSE Collector Bias if SE1 had different collector Bias setting.
\par 12.\tab if Tiff files are saved after the Import Tiff dialog has been displayed then they do not appear in the file list when the import Tiff dialog is redisplayed unless an alternative tab is selected on the Import Tiff dialog.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} V02.03 New Functionality}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} V02.03_New_Functionality}
\pard\keepn \fs36 V02.03 New Functionality
\par \pard \b\fs24 NOTE: If accessed from the installation CD the Links below will fail\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 1.\tab  New File No.,Print No. and HRRU No. parameters which increment with each output. These are in addition to Photo No. which increments for any output. See \uldb \b Counting parameters\plain\b\fs24 {\v DMR0HE@imgmgr.hlp}\plain\fs24 
\par 2.\tab  File save \uldb \b filename format\plain\b\fs24 {\v F7ZT7A@imgmgr.hlp}\plain\fs24  now includes 7 digit file Number.
\par 3.\tab  \uldb \b Print Setup dialog\plain\b\fs24 {\v DVXXAS@imgmgr.hlp}\plain\fs24  now includes Print No.
\par 4.\tab  \uldb \b HRRU Settings\plain\b\fs24 {\v 12O7D55@imgmgr.hlp}\plain\fs24  now includes HRRU No.
\par 5.\tab  Users may now define (on the \uldb \b annotation properties General tab\plain\b\fs24 {\v FZXMV@imgmgr.hlp}\plain\fs24 ) whether to display results to 3,4 or 5 significant figures
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 6.\tab  New \uldb \b string parameters\plain\b\fs24 {\v 6K4IZJ@imgmgr.hlp}\plain\fs24  - File Name, User Name, Operator, User Text for use with annotation.
\par 7.\tab Stage Administrator added for Service use only.
\par 8.\tab \uldb \b Stage Control (navigation)\plain\b\fs24 {\v .QDRS7@stgmgr.hlp}\plain\fs24  now indicates position of Stage door
\par 9.\tab Stage Control (navigation) Middle button click on sample graphic brings point to centre using rotation.
\par 10.\tab LEO 1400 and 1400VP Series: \uldb \b Auto Saturation\plain\b\fs24 {\v 2JVZZU3@dlgmgr.hlp}\plain\fs24  for Tungsten Filaments.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 11.\tab The Macro Editor now contains a menu function (Debug - stop all macros) which may be used to abort all currently running macros.
\par 12.\tab The macro instruction \b End Macro\plain\fs24  has been extended so that it may abort macros other than itself. This has been used in the default \b Resume Exchange\plain\fs24  airlock macro for the 1500 Series to abort the \b Specimen Change\plain\fs24  macro as a means of allowing the user to change his mind once specimen exchange has started. Users who have customised the macro may wish to add this instruction.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 13.\tab Users with the Advanced Measurement Licence now have two additional \uldb \b Radial Measurement\plain\b\fs24 {\v 3BI2_Y0@imgmgr.hlp}\plain\fs24  objects.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} V02.03 Changes}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} V02.03_Changes}
\pard\keepn \fs36 V02.03 Changes 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \fs24 1.\tab The Dual Joystick and Hard Panel may now both be used. N.B. if a dual Joystick is fitted it will be necessary to select it in the Administrator Configuration Stage Tab.
\par 2.\tab Image load. Load area indicator is switched off after load unless step frame is active.
\par 3.\tab Improved performance of Image Gallery
\par 4.\tab Stage Type and stage motorisation parameters now require supervisor privilege.
\par 5.\tab Save/Load Tiff dialogs: User text box now has scroll bar.
\par 6.\tab On 1500 Series only: Crosshairs are now optionally available in emission mode(see User Preferences).
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 7.\tab On 1500 Series only: New Filament setting is now a Service only function. After selecting New Filament the gun operation is disabled until Data from Tip Data Sheet has been entered.
\par 8.\tab Radial Measurement objects now have a centre mark.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} V02.03 Actions required on installation}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} V02.03_Actions_required_on_installation}
\pard\keepn \fs36 V02.03 Actions required on installation
\par \pard \b\fs24 Service Action (1400 and 1500 series only).
\par \plain\fs24 The dual joystick and Hard Panel may now both be used.
\par In the Leo-32 Administrator Configuration Stage tab there is now a checkbox to indicate if the dual joystick is present.
\par In earlier versions the setting of Hard Panel = Absent was used to infer that a Joystick was present, this is no longer the case, hence if a dual joystick is fitted and the checkbox remains unchecked then the joystick will cease to function.
\par 
\par \b User Action.\plain\fs24 
\par \pard To ensure that the latest macros are installed:
\par For each existing User Directory:
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \f5 \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\f2 \tab Select '\b Tools\plain\fs24 ' - '\b Macro Editor\plain\fs24 '
\par \f5 \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\f2 \tab In Macro editor menu select '\b Library\plain\fs24 ' - '\b Merge Standard\plain\fs24 '
\par 
\par \b NOTE\plain\fs24 : A reminder will be given when logging on if this is not done.
\par 
\par If upgrading from a version earlier than V02.02 see \uldb \b V02.01 installation actions\plain\b\fs24 {\v V02.01_Actions_required_on_Installation}\plain\fs24 .
\par \page
